      {
        "id": "p39-q28-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$x-\\frac{4}{x}=3.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$ or $x=-1$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-4&=3x\\\\x^2-3x-4&=0\\\\(x-4)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=4\\text{ or }x=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q29-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$2x+\\frac{1}{x}=3.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac12$ or $x=1$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+1&=3x\\\\2x^2-3x+1&=0\\\\(2x-1)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=\\frac12\\text{ or }x=1.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q30-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$3x-\\frac{2}{x}=4.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}{3}$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $x$, then use the quadratic formula.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x^2-2&=4x\\\\3x^2-4x-2&=0\\\\x&=\\frac{-(-4)\\pm\\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(3)(-2)}}{2(3)}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{40}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm\\sqrt{10}}3.\\end{align*}$$\nNeither value is zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q31-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$x+\\frac1x=\\frac9{10}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No real solutions.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne0$. Multiply by $10x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}10x^2+10&=9x\\\\10x^2-9x+10&=0\\\\b^2-4ac&=(-9)^2-4(10)(10)\\\\b^2-4ac&=-319.\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic formula requires the square root of a negative number, so there are no real solutions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
